mixin () {
  /// Returns static Markdown documentation for the NeoFlow dashboard API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# NeoFlow Dashboard API\n\nRead-only backend for the NeoFlow digital-banking dashboard prototype. It serves the account balance, the monthly expense series for the bar chart, and the ordered quick-action menu. All three methods are `query` calls: they read fixed in-canister data, never mutate state, and are safe to poll or retry.\n\n## Methods\n\n### `getBalance() : async Balance`\n\nReturns the single account balance shown on the dashboard.\n\n- `title : Text` — account display name, e.g. `\"Main Account\"`.\n- `amountCents : Nat` — balance in **EUR cents**; `425000` means `4250.00 EUR`.\n- `currency : Text` — ISO 4217 code, always `\"EUR\"`.\n\n### `getMonthlyExpenses() : async [MonthlyExpense]`\n\nReturns the monthly expense totals that back the bar chart, ordered **oldest to newest**.\n\n- `month : Text` — short month label, e.g. `\"May\"`.\n- `amountCents : Nat` — total expenses for that month, in **EUR cents**.\n\nThe array is a fixed-length series; render bars in the returned order.\n\n### `getQuickActions() : async [QuickAction]`\n\nReturns the fixed, ordered quick-action menu.\n\n- `id : Text` — stable identifier, e.g. `\"send\"`.\n- `title : Text` — display label, e.g. `\"Send\"`.\n- `icon : Text` — icon name the frontend maps to an icon component.\n\nOrder is significant: `Send`, `Receive`, `Pay`, `History`.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\nAll three methods are public `query` functions and require **no authentication** — they return the same fixed prototype data to anonymous and signed-in callers alike. There is no per-user data, no owner scoping, and no admin-only surface in this API.\n\nThe canister also carries the shared authorization mixin used by the app. Its role-guarded endpoints are unrelated to the dashboard reads above; a caller that has never registered through the app frontend is unregistered, and a principal derived against a different Internet Identity derivation origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. The app frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- **Money** is always integer **EUR cents** (`Nat`), never a float. Divide by 100 for display; `425000` → `€4,250.00`.\n- **Timestamps**: this API exposes none.\n- **Identifiers** are plain `Text` (`id`, `month`, `currency`).\n- **Optionals**: none of the returned fields are optional; every field is always present.\n- **Variants**: none; all returned values are plain records and arrays.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nThere is no lifecycle to observe: the data is static, so a single call returns the final value. Polling is unnecessary; if the UI refreshes, re-calling any method is cheap and returns identical results. There are no state transitions and no completion conditions to wait on.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\nAll three methods are read-only `query` calls. They never write state, so retrying them is always safe and idempotent, and there are no destructive effects or duplicate-call hazards.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- These methods do not trap under normal use; they return fixed data.\n- `amountCents` is a `Nat` of cents — do not treat it as a decimal amount or as a float.\n- The expense series and quick-action list are fixed-length; do not assume a specific length, iterate the returned array.\n- This is a **sandbox educational prototype** and an unregulated simulation. It is not a real banking service and must not be used for actual financial activity.\n";
  };
};
